      <section>
        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

        <h3>What does a supply chain management expert do?</h3>

        <p>
          Supply chain management experts help businesses improve procurement,
          supplier management, sourcing, quality, delivery, risk management and other
          parts of the supply chain. Their role depends on the company's specific
          requirements.
        </p>

        <h3>What is the difference between procurement and supply chain management?</h3>

        <p>
          Procurement focuses primarily on acquiring products, materials and services,
          while supply chain management takes a broader view of how suppliers,
          purchasing, production, inventory, logistics and information work together.
        </p>

        <h3>When should a company hire a supply chain consultant?</h3>

        <p>
          Companies may benefit from external supply chain expertise when they face
          supplier problems, rising procurement costs, quality issues, supply
          disruptions, supplier concentration or expansion into new products and
          markets.
        </p>

        <h3>Can a supply chain expert help with China suppliers?</h3>

        <p>
          Yes. Supply chain experts with China sourcing experience can help businesses
          evaluate manufacturers, develop suppliers, assess sourcing risks and improve
          communication with Chinese suppliers.
        </p>

        <h3>Does a business need a full-time supply chain expert?</h3>

        <p>
          Not necessarily. Some businesses need ongoing supply chain management, while
          others may only need external expertise for supplier development, sourcing,
          risk assessment or a specific procurement project.
        </p>
